    slot: '주제',
    body: '다음 글의 주제로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">Many people take pride in their ability to handle several tasks at once, writing a report while replying to messages and listening in on a meeting. It feels efficient, but what we call multitasking is usually something else. For tasks that require attention, the brain rapidly switches back and forth between them rather than truly doing them at the same time. Each switch has a price. When we return to a task, we must recall where we left off, what we were trying to do, and which rules apply, and this takes time even if we do not notice it. Studies of task switching have found that people who alternate between tasks tend to be slower and to make more errors than when they complete the same tasks one after another. The small delays add up, and the feeling of being productive hides the real loss.</div>',
