    slot: '주장',
    body: '다음 글에서 필자가 주장하는 바로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">In many cities, public benches are quietly disappearing. Some are removed because officials worry that people will stay too long; others are replaced with narrow seats that are uncomfortable to sit on for more than a few minutes. The goal is to keep sidewalks moving and tidy, but the cost falls on those who most need a place to rest. An elderly person walking to the market may need to stop several times along the way. A parent carrying a tired child, a worker on a short break, or someone recovering from an injury all depend on a place to sit down. Without benches, many of these people simply stay home, and the street loses the very people who make it lively. A city is not only a route from one place to another; it is also a place to be. City planners should provide enough comfortable seating in public spaces so that everyone can use the streets.</div>',
