    body: '다음 글에서 필자가 주장하는 바로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">When a shocking story appears on our screens, the urge to pass it on is almost immediate. We want to warn our friends, show that we are informed, or simply share our surprise. With a single tap, the story reaches dozens of people, and each of them can send it to dozens more. Unfortunately, false stories often spread faster than true ones, partly because they are designed to provoke strong feelings. Once a rumor has traveled widely, a correction rarely catches up with it, and many of the people who shared it never see the correction at all. This is why each of us now has a responsibility that we did not have when news came only from newspapers and television. Before sharing a story, we should take a moment to check where it came from, whether other reliable sources report the same thing, and when it was published. A few seconds of checking can stop a falsehood from reaching thousands of people.</div>',
