    slot: '주제',
    body: '다음 글의 주제로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">While their seeds are still developing, many fruits are green, hard, and sour or bitter. This is no accident. A seed that is eaten before it is mature cannot grow into a new plant, so it pays for the parent plant to make its unripe fruit hard to see against the leaves and unpleasant to eat. Once the seeds are ready, the situation changes completely. The fruit softens, its starches turn into sugars, and its skin often becomes red, orange, yellow, or purple, standing out clearly against the green background. These changes act as an invitation. Birds and mammals eat the sweet fruit and later drop the seeds, often far from the parent plant, where the young plants will not have to compete with it for light and water. In this way, the plant turns hungry animals into partners that carry its offspring to new places.</div>',
