    body: '글의 흐름으로 보아, 주어진 문장이 들어가기에 가장 적절한 곳은?<div class="bogi">It therefore settles into the water only until the water it pushes aside weighs as much as the ship itself, and then it floats.</div><div class="passage">A solid block of steel dropped into the sea sinks immediately, yet ships made of thousands of tons of steel float. ( ① ) The explanation lies in a principle first described by the ancient Greek scientist Archimedes. ( ② ) An object placed in water pushes some of the water aside, and the water pushes back with an upward force equal to the weight of the water that has been pushed aside. ( ③ ) A steel block takes up little space for its weight, so it cannot push aside enough water to hold itself up. ( ④ ) A ship’s hull, however, is shaped like a huge bowl filled mostly with air, so it takes up a very large volume while weighing relatively little for its size. ( ⑤ ) This is also why a ship that takes on water through a hole is in danger: as water replaces the air inside, the ship grows heavier without growing larger, and it begins to sink.</div>',
