    body: '다음 글의 내용을 한 문장으로 요약할 때, 빈칸 (A), (B)에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">In a classic set of experiments, researchers gave participants pairs of related words to study. For some pairs, participants simply read both words, such as “hot − cold.” For others, they were given the first word and only the first letter of the second, as in “hot − c___,” and had to produce the missing word themselves. The task was easy, and the words they ended up with were the same as those in the reading condition. Yet on a later memory test, participants remembered the words they had produced better than the ones they had only read. This advantage has since been found with many kinds of material. Even a small amount of effort to come up with information, it seems, leaves a deeper trace in memory than receiving the same information ready-made.</div><div class="bogi">Information that people <b>(A)</b> on their own tends to be <b>(B)</b> better than the same information simply given to them.</div>',
