    body: '다음 글의 내용을 한 문장으로 요약할 때, 빈칸 (A), (B)에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">In a well-known experiment, some students in a class were given coffee mugs, while the others received nothing. The students with mugs were asked the lowest price at which they would sell theirs, and the students without mugs were asked the highest price they would pay to buy one. Since the mugs had been handed out at random, the two groups should have valued them about equally. Instead, the owners typically demanded roughly twice as much as the buyers were willing to pay, and far fewer trades took place than expected. Owning the mug for only a few minutes seemed to have changed how much it was worth to them. Similar results have been found with many other everyday items. Giving something up, it appears, feels like a loss, and people demand extra compensation for that loss.</div><div class="bogi">Simply <b>(A)</b> an object can lead people to <b>(B)</b> it more highly than they would if it were not theirs.</div>',
