    body: '다음 글의 밑줄 친 부분 중, 어법상 <b>틀린</b> 것은?<div class="passage">Keeping a daily journal is one of the simplest habits a person can develop, yet its benefits are often underestimated. Writing for only a few minutes each evening <u>① gives</u> you a chance to look back on the day and notice what went well and what did not. Many people find that problems <u>② what</u> seemed overwhelming in the afternoon look much smaller once they are put into words. The act of writing forces us <u>③ to slow</u> down and choose our words, which in turn helps us organize our thoughts. Over months and years, a journal also becomes a record of how we have changed, <u>④ allowing</u> us to see patterns that would be invisible from day to day. You do not need special skills or expensive notebooks to begin; all that <u>⑤ is</u> required is a pen, a few pages, and the willingness to be honest with yourself.</div>',
