    subject: 'eng',
    unit: 'reading',
    kind: 'real',
    points: 3,
    level: 3,
    slot: '어휘',
    body: '다음 글의 밑줄 친 부분 중, 문맥상 낱말의 쓰임이 적절하지 <b>않은</b> 것은?<div class="passage">When people estimate how long a project will take, they are remarkably likely to be too <u>① pessimistic</u>. Students expect to finish their essays days before the deadline, and builders promise that a new bridge will open next spring, yet the work frequently runs late. This happens even when people know that similar tasks took them longer in the past. The reason is that we tend to imagine the project as a <u>② smooth</u> series of steps, focusing on the specific plan in front of us rather than on what usually happens. Interruptions, illness, and unexpected problems seem <u>③ unlikely</u> when we think about our own case, even though something of the kind almost always occurs. One useful remedy is to <u>④ set aside</u> the details of the current plan for a moment and ask how long comparable projects have actually taken. This outside view tends to produce more <u>⑤ realistic</u> estimates, because it automatically includes the delays we forget to imagine.</div>',
