    body: '글의 흐름으로 보아, 주어진 문장이 들어가기에 가장 적절한 곳은?<div class="bogi">Water is a striking exception: it expands as it freezes, so ice is less dense than the liquid around it.</div><div class="passage">( ① ) In winter, a lake does not freeze solid all at once. ( ② ) A thin sheet of ice appears first at the surface, and it then acts as a lid, insulating the water beneath it from the freezing air above. ( ③ ) Fish and other organisms can therefore survive the winter in the liquid water near the bottom, where the temperature stays a few degrees above freezing. ( ④ ) This familiar pattern is stranger than it looks. Most substances become denser as they cool and solidify, so their solid forms sink in their own liquids. ( ⑤ ) Had water followed the same rule, ice would sink as it formed, lakes would freeze from the bottom up, and many would turn almost entirely solid during a cold season, leaving little room for the creatures that live in them. The odd behavior of a single substance, in other words, helps make life in cold climates possible.</div>',
