    slot: '빈칸 추론 · 고난도',
    body: '다음 빈칸에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">Many people treat the dictionary as a court of law: if a word is used in a way the dictionary does not list, the usage is simply wrong. Yet lexicographers themselves rarely see their work this way. A dictionary entry is built by collecting thousands of examples of a word in actual use — in newspapers, novels, letters, and conversations — and then describing the patterns found in them. When enough speakers begin to use a word in a new sense, that sense eventually appears in a later edition, not because an authority has approved it, but because the evidence can no longer be ignored. The English word <i>nice</i>, for example, once meant “foolish” before drifting through several senses to its present meaning of “pleasant,” and no dictionary could have stopped that journey. In this sense, a dictionary is less a rulebook than a ________: it tells us where the language has been, not where it must go.</div>',
