    slot: '빈칸 추론 · 고난도',
    body: '다음 빈칸에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">When a non-native species takes over an ecosystem, the obvious response is to remove it. Sometimes, however, removal does more harm than the invader ever did. Consider an island where introduced rats have lived for over a century. Native birds may have declined, but the island’s hawks may now depend on the rats as their main prey, and certain native plants may rely on the rats to scatter their seeds. Eliminate the rats suddenly, and the hawks may turn to the few remaining native birds, while the plants lose the disperser they have come to depend on. In other cases, an invasive shrub that crowds out native vegetation may also have become the preferred nesting site of an endangered songbird. Such examples do not mean that invaders should be left alone. They mean that, after long enough, an invader is no longer simply an outsider; it has ________, and pulling it out tears the threads that others now hang on.</div>',
