    body: '글의 흐름으로 보아, 주어진 문장이 들어가기에 가장 적절한 곳은?<div class="bogi">Each fire put out, however, left behind the dead branches and undergrowth that it would otherwise have consumed.</div><div class="passage">For much of the twentieth century, forest managers in many countries treated every wildfire as an enemy to be extinguished as quickly as possible. ( ① ) Their efforts were impressively effective, and the area burned each year fell sharply. ( ② ) Over the decades, this material piled up on the forest floor, turning forests that had once burned lightly and often into vast stores of fuel. ( ③ ) When a fire finally escaped control under hot, dry conditions, it no longer crept along the ground but climbed into the crowns of the trees and burned with an intensity those forests had rarely known. ( ④ ) In trying to eliminate fire, managers had unintentionally ensured that the fires that did occur would be far more destructive. ( ⑤ ) This is why many ecologists now argue that small, carefully controlled burns are needed to restore the older pattern.</div>',
