    level: 5,
    slot: '빈칸 추론 · 고난도',
    body: '다음 빈칸에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">Organizations reward what they can see. A team that launches a new product receives praise, a larger budget, and perhaps a promotion; a team that quietly replaces aging pipes so that a factory never floods receives almost nothing. The difference is not that the second team has contributed less. It is that its contribution takes the form of an event that never occurs. Nobody celebrates the flood that did not happen, because nobody experiences it. Worse, the better preventive work is done, the more unnecessary it appears: years without failure lead managers to conclude that the risk was exaggerated, and the maintenance budget is the first to be cut. In this way, the success of prevention ________. Only after the neglected system finally breaks does its value become visible, and by then the cost of repair is far greater than the cost of care would have been.</div>',
