    slot: '글의 순서 · 고난도',
    body: '주어진 글 다음에 이어질 글의 순서로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">Look at a map of the world’s great trading cities, and a pattern appears: many of them stand where one form of transport gives way to another.</div><div class="passage">(A) Each of these activities required workers, and workers required housing, food, and services. A settlement that began as a stopping point thus grew, step by step, into a city whose size had little to do with the quality of the land around it.<br>(B) A river mouth where ocean ships met river boats, or a harbor where cargo left ships for wagons, forced goods to stop. They had to be unloaded, stored, and often sorted or sold before they could continue their journey.<br>(C) This logic also explains why some of these cities declined once the pattern of transport changed. When railways or larger ships allowed goods to pass straight through without being unloaded, the activities that had sustained the city began to disappear.</div>',
