    body: '다음 빈칸에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">When a cracked vase or a damaged painting arrives in a conservation studio today, the restorer’s aim is no longer to make it look as if nothing had ever happened. For centuries, that was exactly the goal: missing pieces were carved anew, faded colors were repainted, and the finished object was presented as whole. The trouble was that later viewers could no longer tell where the original ended and the repair began, and many celebrated works turned out to be partly the creation of anonymous craftsmen who had guessed at what the artist intended. Modern practice therefore follows a different principle. Gaps are filled in a slightly different tone, visible on close inspection though not from across the room, and every material added must be removable without harm to what remains. The restorer, in other words, must ________. An honest repair is one that a future expert can find, judge, and, if necessary, undo.</div>',
