    body: '글의 흐름으로 보아, 주어진 문장이 들어가기에 가장 적절한 곳은?<div class="bogi">Yet by every test researchers have devised, most octopuses appear to be colorblind.</div><div class="passage">Few animals change their appearance as quickly or as convincingly as the octopus. ( ① ) Within a fraction of a second, it can shift its skin from mottled brown to sandy gray, matching not only the color of the rocks or weeds around it but often their texture as well. ( ② ) Such skill naturally suggests a keen sense of color, since an animal that matches its background must, one would think, be able to see it. ( ③ ) Their eyes contain only one type of light-sensitive pigment, which should allow them to tell bright from dark but not one hue from another. ( ④ ) This puzzle has led to several proposals. ( ⑤ ) One is that the skin itself may detect light, since proteins similar to those in the eye have been found there; another is that the unusual shape of the octopus’s pupil may let it extract color information in a way no one yet fully understands.</div>',
