    body: '다음 글에서 전체 흐름과 관계 <b>없는</b> 문장은?<div class="passage">When a honeybee forager discovers a rich patch of flowers, she returns to the hive and performs what is known as the waggle dance. ① She runs a short straight line across the vertical surface of the comb while shaking her body, then circles back and repeats the run, sometimes dozens of times. ② Because the comb hangs vertically, worker bees build each cell tilted slightly upward, which keeps the honey stored inside from flowing out. ③ The angle of the straight run relative to vertical indicates the direction of the flowers relative to the sun, and the length of the run indicates their distance. ④ Other bees follow the dancer closely, sensing her movements in the darkness of the hive, and then fly out to search the area she has described. ⑤ Remarkably, the message stays accurate over the course of a day, because foragers adjust the angle of their dance as the sun moves across the sky.</div>',
