    level: 4,
    slot: '어법 · 고난도',
    body: '다음 글의 밑줄 친 부분 중, 어법상 <b>틀린</b> 것은?<div class="passage">It seems strange that people <u>① choose</u> to live on the slopes of active volcanoes, where an eruption could destroy their homes at any moment. Yet the slopes of volcanoes such as Etna and Vesuvius have been farmed for thousands of years, and the reason lies in the ground itself. Volcanic ash, <u>② which</u> is rich in minerals such as potassium and phosphorus, breaks down quickly into soil that crops find highly fertile. A field that <u>③ have been covered</u> by a thin layer of ash may become more productive within a few years than it was before. Farmers <u>④ whose</u> families have worked such land for generations often regard the risk of eruption as a fair price for the harvests it brings. The volcano, in their view, is not only a threat but also the source of the very soil that <u>⑤ sustains</u> them.</div>',
