    slot: '함축 의미 · 고난도',
    body: '밑줄 친 부분이 다음 글에서 의미하는 바로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">On a big mountain, the moment of reaching the top is the one climbers remember, photograph, and celebrate. Yet the top is also where they are most tired, lowest on oxygen and daylight, and furthest from safety. The way down demands the same care as the way up, usually with less strength left to give it, and exhausted climbers are prone to careless mistakes on the descent. This is why experienced expedition leaders fix a turnaround time before the climb begins: if the team has not reached the summit by, say, two in the afternoon, it turns back, however close the top may look. Setting the rule in advance matters, because high on the mountain, with the goal in sight after weeks of effort, almost no one can judge clearly whether to go on. Among climbers the lesson is summed up in a short phrase: <u>the summit is only halfway</u>. A climb is judged not by whether the top was reached but by whether everyone came home, and a plan that spends all its strength on getting up has failed before it starts.</div>',
