    body: '밑줄 친 부분이 다음 글에서 의미하는 바로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">Gardeners who grow flowers for competitions know a trick that looks wasteful to beginners. When a stem forms several buds, they pinch off all but one, removing buds that are perfectly healthy. The plant’s energy, no longer divided among many flowers, flows into the single bud that remains, and it opens far larger than it otherwise would. Beginners find this hard because the buds they remove are not weak or diseased. Cutting away a dead branch is easy; cutting away a living one feels like destroying something of value. The same reluctance appears wherever effort is limited. A writer keeps a paragraph because it is well written, even though the essay would be stronger without it; a team keeps a promising project going alongside three others, and all four move slowly. Removing what is bad requires only judgment. Removing what is good but not the best requires the harder discipline of accepting a loss. Anyone who wants one excellent result rather than many ordinary ones must <u>learn to cut living wood</u>.</div>',
