    body: '다음 빈칸에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">Ecologists once measured a predator’s effect on its prey mainly by counting the animals it killed. If wolves took a certain number of deer each winter, that number was the predator’s impact. But the deer that survive also pay a price. Where predators are present, prey animals spend more time watching for danger and less time eating; they avoid rich feeding grounds that offer no escape; some even produce fewer young. In one experiment, song sparrows were exposed only to recorded calls of their predators, with no actual hunting taking place, and they raised noticeably fewer offspring than sparrows that heard the calls of harmless animals. The fear alone was enough. A predator’s most far-reaching effect, then, may lie not in the animals it eats but in ________.</div>',
