    body: '다음 글의 빈칸 (A), (B)에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">Fresh snow and sea ice reflect most of the sunlight that strikes them back into space, while open ocean water, being dark, absorbs most of it. This difference sets up a powerful cycle in the Arctic. When warmer temperatures melt some of the ice, more dark water is exposed. (A) ________, the ocean absorbs more of the sun’s energy, warms further, and melts still more ice. Scientists call such a self-reinforcing cycle a positive feedback. The word “positive” here can be misleading. It does not mean that the effect is good; it means only that a change, once started, pushes itself further in the same direction. (B) ________, a negative feedback works against the original change, the way a thermostat switches off a heater once a room is warm enough, bringing the system back toward balance.</div>',
