    slot: '장문 세트 (1/3) 순서 · 고난도',
    body: '[1~3] 다음 글을 읽고, 물음에 답하시오.<div class="passage">(A)<br>Hana had known for a year that this Saturday would come, and now that it had, she wished it would never end. Twelve months earlier, her family had agreed to raise a puppy for a guide dog school. The puppy, a yellow Labrador named Biscuit, had chewed two of Hana’s shoes, learned to sit before <u>(a) she</u> could finish saying the word, and slept every night at the foot of her bed. Today Biscuit was going back to the school to begin his real training.<br>(B)<br>Eight months later, a letter arrived from the school: Biscuit had completed his training, and his puppy-raising family was invited to the graduation ceremony. There Hana saw him again, wearing a harness beside a young man named Daniel, who had lost his sight in an accident. When Biscuit noticed Hana, his tail swung wildly, but he stayed at Daniel’s side. <u>(d) She</u> felt proud and a little heartbroken at the same time. On the drive home, Hana was quiet for a long time. Then <u>(e) she</u> asked her mother whether the school might need someone to raise another puppy.<br>(C)<br>At the school, a trainer named Ms. Park met the family at the gate. <u>(b) She</u> knelt to greet Biscuit, who rolled onto his back as if they were old friends. Hana held the leash a moment longer than she needed to. “He knows a lot of things,” she said, and then could not remember any of them. Ms. Park smiled and waited until Hana was ready to let go.<br>(D)<br>As Biscuit was led away, he looked back once, and Hana turned her face into her mother’s coat. Ms. Park did not tell her not to cry. Instead, she explained that the dogs who do best in training are often the ones who have been loved the most, because they have learned to trust people. “Whatever he learns here,” Ms. Park said, “he’ll be building on the year he spent with you.” Hearing this, Hana wiped <u>(c) her</u> eyes and managed a small smile.</div>주어진 글 (A)에 이어질 내용을 순서에 맞게 배열한 것으로 가장 적절한 것은?',
    type: 'choice',
    choices: ['(B) - (D) - (C)', '(C) - (B) - (D)', '(C) - (D) - (B)', '(D) - (B) - (C)', '(D) - (C) - (B)'],
    answer: 3,
    concepts: ['e-order'],
    hint: 'Ms. Park이 처음 소개되는 단락은? ‘Eight months later’는 언제를 기준으로 한 말일까요?',
    solution:
      '<ol class="sol-steps"><li>(A) 끝: 오늘 Biscuit이 학교로 돌아간다 → 학교에 도착한 장면 (C) <i>At the school, a trainer named Ms. Park met the family</i>(Ms. Park 첫 소개, 이름 앞에 a trainer named).</li><li>(C) 끝: Hana가 목줄을 놓을 준비가 될 때까지 기다림 → (D) <i>As Biscuit was led away</i>(목줄을 넘긴 뒤 데려감), Ms. Park의 위로.</li><li>(D) 이후 → (B) <i>Eight months later</i> 졸업식, 마지막에 또 다른 강아지를 키우고 싶다는 결말 → (C)-(D)-(B) ③</li><li>(D)가 (C)보다 먼저 오면 Ms. Park이 소개도 없이 등장해요. (B)가 앞에 오면 졸업식 뒤에 다시 헤어지는 장면이 와서 시간이 거꾸로 가요.</li></ol><div class="sol-ans">답: <b>③</b></div><div class="sol-warn"><b>많이 틀리는 곳</b> (D)-(C)-(B)를 고르는 학생이 있어요. (A) 끝의 going back에서 바로 ‘데려가는’ 장면을 떠올린 거예요. 하지만 Ms. Park을 처음 소개하는 문장(a trainer named)은 (C)에만 있어요.<br><b>1등급 전략</b> 장문 순서는 인물이 ‘처음 소개되는 표현’(a/named)과 시간 표현(later)을 먼저 찾아 고정하세요.</div>',
    mistakes: ['(D)-(C)-(B) 고르기: 인물 첫 소개 단서 놓침', '(B)를 앞에 두기: Eight months later의 기준 시점 혼동'],
