    slot: '빈칸 추론 · 고난도',
    body: '다음 빈칸에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">Suppose that somewhere in the world a new use is found for a certain metal, or that a mine which produced much of it suddenly closes. The price of the metal rises. Across the world, thousands of factories that depend on it respond: some switch to substitutes, some use it more sparingly, and some postpone projects that would need large amounts of it. Remarkably, almost none of them know why the price has risen, and they do not need to. A planner trying to produce the same result would have to learn where the metal was needed most, which users could do without it, and how much each would lose by giving it up, information scattered across millions of minds and changing every day. The price compresses all of this into a single number. It does not explain the shortage; it simply tells each user how seriously to take it. In this sense, the price system works less like a command than like a signal, and its great strength is that it ________.</div>',
    type: 'choice',
