    slot: '빈칸 추론 · 고난도',
    body: '다음 빈칸에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">It is tempting to describe the traits of living things as solutions designed for the problems they face. The thick fur of an arctic fox or the long neck of a giraffe seems to anticipate exactly what its owner will need. But natural selection has no foresight. A trait spreads only because individuals that had it left more offspring than those that lacked it, under the conditions in which their ancestors lived. If those conditions change faster than selection can follow, the same trait may become useless or even harmful. Birds that evolved on islands without predators, for example, often lost their fear of large animals, and some lost the ability to fly; when people arrived with dogs, cats, and rats, these birds were among the first to disappear. Nothing had gone wrong with them. Their bodies and habits were doing precisely what they had been shaped to do, in a world that no longer existed. Every adaptation, in this sense, is ________.</div>',
    type: 'choice',
    choices: [
      'a compromise between the needs of the individual and the species',
      'a record of the past rather than a forecast of the future',
      'evidence that the environment has never changed',
      'a response to the needs that an organism will face later',
      'an error that natural selection will eventually correct',
    ],
    answer: 2,
    concepts: ['e-blank'],
    hint: '섬의 새들이 사라진 건 몸에 문제가 있어서였나요? 그 몸은 ‘언제’의 세계에 맞춰져 있었나요?',
    solution:
      '<ol class="sol-steps"><li><i>natural selection has no foresight</i> → 앞날을 내다보지 않아요.</li><li><i>under the conditions in which their ancestors lived</i> → 형질은 조상이 살던 조건에서 퍼져요.</li><li><i>doing precisely what they had been shaped to do, in a world that no longer existed</i> → 적응은 지나간 환경에 대한 기록 → ②</li><li>④ 앞으로 닥칠 필요에 대한 대응 = 글이 부정하는 생각(첫 두 문장). ⑤ <i>Nothing had gone wrong</i>과 충돌. ③ 글은 조건이 바뀐다(<i>If those conditions change</i>)고 했어요. ① 개체와 종의 타협은 나오지 않아요.</li></ol><div class="sol-ans">답: <b>②</b></div><div class="sol-warn"><b>많이 틀리는 곳</b> ④는 첫 두 문장(<i>seems to anticipate</i>)을 그대로 옮긴 선지예요. 글쓴이가 <i>But</i>으로 뒤집은 통념이에요.<br><b>1등급 전략</b> ‘It is tempting to …’로 시작하면 통념 → 반박 구조예요. 빈칸은 반박 쪽 핵심(no foresight, a world that no longer existed)을 받아요.</div>',
