    body: '다음 빈칸에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">Imagine that a painting long admired as the work of a famous master is revealed to be a forgery, made centuries later by a skilled imitator. Not a single brushstroke has changed. The colors are as rich as they were the day before, and the composition is just as balanced. Yet the museum moves the painting to storage, and visitors who once stood before it in silence would now give it a curious glance at most. It is easy to call this snobbery, as if people had only ever been admiring a famous name. But the reaction makes sense if we accept that looking at a painting has never been only a matter of what reaches the eye. When we admire a work, we admire it as an achievement: as the solution, by a particular person at a particular moment, to problems that no one had solved before. The forger solved a different and much smaller problem, namely how to copy a solution that already existed. What has changed, then, is not the object but ________.</div>',
