    body: '다음 빈칸에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">We like to think of knowledge as something each of us has earned for ourselves. Yet consider how much of what you know you have never checked. You believe that the Earth orbits the Sun, that your grandparents were born where you were told, and that the medicine in your cabinet contains what its label says, but in almost every case your evidence is simply that someone told you. If knowledge required personal verification, nearly all of it would vanish, and so would science itself, since no researcher can repeat every experiment on which her own work depends. This does not mean that we should believe whatever we hear. It means that the crucial intellectual skill is not checking everything oneself but ________. A good thinker resembles less a lone explorer than a shrewd manager of other people’s expertise.</div>',
