    body: '주어진 글 다음에 이어질 글의 순서로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">Young children learning English often say <i>went</i> correctly, and then, a few months later, begin to say <i>goed</i> instead.</div><div class="passage">(A) Only later, as they keep hearing <i>went</i> from the people around them, do they learn that this verb is an exception, and <i>went</i> returns, this time as a word that is known to break the rule.<br>(B) To parents, this looks like a step backward. But the error is in fact a sign of progress. At first, <i>went</i> is simply memorized as a single word, with no connection to any rule.<br>(C) Then children discover the pattern that most verbs form the past by adding <i>-ed</i>, and they begin to apply it everywhere, even to verbs that do not follow it. The new rule temporarily overpowers the memorized word.</div>',
    type: 'choice',
