    body: '글의 흐름으로 보아, 주어진 문장이 들어가기에 가장 적절한 곳은?<div class="bogi">Adding the statistics, however, did not add to their concern but took away from it: they gave less than those who had read about the girl alone.</div><div class="passage">Charities have long known that a single face moves people more than a large number. ( ① ) In one study, people were asked to give money after reading either about a particular seven-year-old girl facing hunger or about the millions of people facing food shortages in a region of Africa. ( ② ) Those who read about the girl gave far more. ( ③ ) More surprisingly, a third group read about the girl together with the statistics describing the wider crisis. ( ④ ) Why should more information produce less giving? One possibility is that thinking about numbers shifted people into a calculating frame of mind, in which the feeling that drives generosity grew weaker. ( ⑤ ) The result is an uncomfortable fact about human compassion: the larger a tragedy becomes, the harder it may be for us to feel it.</div>',
