    body: '글의 흐름으로 보아, 주어진 문장이 들어가기에 가장 적절한 곳은?<div class="bogi">The new word, however, soon picks up the very associations it was meant to escape.</div><div class="passage">( ① ) Words for things that make people uncomfortable rarely stay polite for long. ( ② ) When a term for an illness, a disability, or an unpleasant job comes to sound harsh, people replace it with a gentler one. ( ③ ) This cycle continues because what makes a word sound harsh is usually not its sound or its origin but the attitudes people hold toward the thing it names. ( ④ ) As long as those attitudes remain, any word used for that thing will gradually absorb them, and before long it, too, will need replacing. ( ⑤ ) This is why changing a word, however well meant, can rarely do the work of changing the way people think.</div>',
