    slot: '장문 세트 (2/2) 지칭 · 고난도',
    body: '[1~2] 다음 글을 읽고, 물음에 답하시오.<div class="passage">(A)<br>Every Saturday morning, Junho helped at the children’s reading club in the neighborhood library. Most of the children loved taking turns reading aloud, but one boy, Taemin, always shook his head when the book reached him. Even when Junho offered to read along with him, <u>(a) he</u> only stared at the floor. Mr. Han, the librarian who ran the club, had told Junho not to push. “Some children need time,” he had said. So Junho read Taemin’s part for him and moved on, though he could not help wondering what the boy was afraid of.<br>(B)<br>Two weeks later, Taemin arrived wearing a pair of round glasses with blue frames. He sat down without a word, but when the book came around to him, he did not shake his head. He looked at the page for a long time. Then, slowly and carefully, <u>(b) he</u> began to read. His voice was so soft that the other children leaned forward to hear.<br>(C)<br>When Taemin finished his page, nobody said anything for a second, and then one of the girls clapped. Soon everyone was clapping. Taemin’s ears turned red, but he was smiling. As the children were leaving, he stopped at the door and looked back at Junho. “Next week,” <u>(c) he</u> said, “can I read two pages?”<br>(D)<br>One Saturday, Junho noticed something. Whenever Taemin looked at a picture book, <u>(d) he</u> held it very close to his face, and he squinted at the words on the whiteboard as if they were far away. After the club, Junho mentioned this quietly to Mr. Han. The librarian was silent for a moment. Then <u>(e) he</u> picked up the phone and called Taemin’s mother.</div>',
    type: 'choice',
