    body: '다음 빈칸에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">Philosophers who wanted knowledge to be secure have often dreamed of a starting point beyond all doubt: a few certain truths on which everything else could be built, the way a house rests on its foundation. The trouble is that no such truths seem to be available. Every observation we might use as a foundation is itself interpreted in the light of other beliefs, which could also be mistaken. The philosopher Otto Neurath offered a different picture. We are, he said, like sailors who must rebuild their ship on the open sea, never able to bring it into a dock and reconstruct it from the bottom up. A rotten plank can be replaced, but only while the sailors stand on the others, and no plank is safe from being replaced in its turn. On this view, the absence of a firm foundation is not a reason for despair. It simply means that improving what we know is always a matter of ________.</div>',
