    body: '다음 빈칸에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">In a market for used cars, sellers know far more than buyers about the cars they are selling. A buyer cannot tell a well-maintained car from one with hidden faults, so the most she is willing to pay is a price that reflects the average quality she expects. This creates a problem for the owners of good cars. Offered only an average price, many of them decide to keep their cars rather than sell them for less than they are worth, while the owners of bad cars are happy to accept it. As the good cars leave the market, the average quality of the cars still for sale falls, buyers lower the price they will pay, and still more good cars are withdrawn. In the extreme, only the worst cars remain. The striking point of this analysis, first set out by the economist George Akerlof, is that a market can fail even when every buyer wants a good car and every owner of a good car would be glad to sell one at a fair price: what destroys the trade is not a lack of demand or supply but ________.</div>',
