    body: '다음 빈칸에 들어갈 말로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">Flight instructors in one air force once told a psychologist that praise did not work. Whenever they praised a trainee for an exceptionally smooth landing, the next landing was usually worse; whenever they shouted at a trainee after a terrible one, the next was usually better. Criticism, they concluded, was the better teacher. The psychologist saw a different explanation. Any single landing depends partly on skill and partly on luck: a sudden gust of wind, a moment of distraction. An exceptionally good landing is therefore likely to have involved unusually good luck, and an exceptionally bad one unusually bad luck. Since luck does not carry over from one attempt to the next, the following attempt will tend to fall closer to the trainee’s ordinary level, whatever the instructor says. The instructors were not wrong about what they saw; they were wrong about its cause. Because extreme results tend to be followed by more ordinary ones, a teacher who responds only to the extremes will ________.</div>',
