    body: '주어진 글 다음에 이어질 글의 순서로 가장 적절한 것은?<div class="passage">When several companies bid for the right to drill in an oil field, each makes its own estimate of how much oil lies underground. Some estimates will be too high and some too low, but on average they may be quite accurate.</div><div class="passage">(A) Yet that expectation ignores who the winner is. The company that wins is not a typical bidder; it is the one whose estimate was the highest, and therefore, very often, the one that overestimated the most. Winning is itself a sign that the winner has probably paid too much.<br>(B) One might therefore expect an auction, by drawing on all these estimates, to arrive at a fair price for the field, so that the winning company pays roughly what the oil is worth.<br>(C) Experienced bidders have learned to guard against this so-called winner’s curse. They deliberately bid less than their own estimate, and the more rivals they face, the more they hold back, since the highest of many guesses is likely to be a wild one.</div>',
