    level: 4,
    slot: '문장 삽입 · 고난도',
    body: '글의 흐름으로 보아, 주어진 문장이 들어가기에 가장 적절한 곳은?<div class="bogi">The time at the home port was much harder to know, since it had to be carried on board.</div><div class="passage">For centuries, sailors could find their latitude, their position north or south, with little difficulty by measuring the height of the Sun at noon or of the Pole Star at night. ( ① ) Longitude, their position east or west, was another matter. ( ② ) Because the Earth turns through fifteen degrees every hour, the difference between local time and the time at a fixed home port reveals how far east or west a ship has traveled. ( ③ ) Local time was easy to find: noon is the moment the Sun stands highest. ( ④ ) The pendulum clocks of the day, which kept good time on land, were thrown off by the rolling of a ship and by changes in temperature. ( ⑤ ) It was not until the eighteenth century that the English clockmaker John Harrison built a timepiece accurate enough to solve the problem, and even then many astronomers continued to prefer a method based on the position of the Moon.</div>',
